; parity.exe compares the rasterizing rules with rasterio's on tessera-eval's
; Austria labels and GeoTessera's landmask grids. It needs those files and
; rasterio's rasters, which live outside the repository, so no test runs it:
;   parity.exe project DIR   writes DIR/jord_*.npy, the labels in UTM 33N;
;   (rasterio, outside the repository, writes DIR/<tile>.* from them);
;   parity.exe compare DIR   prints the cells where the owners differ.

(executable
 (name parity)
 (libraries jord nx nx.io jsont jsont.bytesrw))
